  "instance_name": "mapping_001",
  "label": "Affectionate but ableist message mapped onto the person",
  "description": "The text 'we wouldn't change him for the world' is mapped onto the visual entity 'person' to create an affectionate tone, while the contrasting text 'but we wish the world would change for him' implies the person's disability requires societal adaptation, thus establishing an analogical mapping between the textual message and the visual subject. The person's joyful expression is juxtaposed with the ableist message, creating a surface-level affection that masks the underlying trope of societal change required.",
